# Core rules (Cursor)

Canonical project brief and hard constraints: **`AGENTS.md`**. Workflow: **`docs/workflow/workflow.md`**.

- **Own worktree + `cursor/<lane>-<slug>` branch.** Open the worktree folder from `scripts/agents/worktree.sh new cursor …` in its own window. Never edit the main checkout. Check `git branch --show-current` before the first edit.
- **Stay in your lane** (`docs/workflow/roles-and-lanes.md`). Other files → cross-lane request via the `scribe` skill.
- **Skills** in `.agents/skills/`: `lane-builder` to execute an assignment, `scribe` for logs and PR bodies (use a fast model), `product-manager` / `senior-qa` when asked.
- **Model per ticket** (`docs/workflow/model-routing.md`): fast model for docs and grunt work, standard for implementation, heavy for planning and unknown bugs. Use best-of-N across model families for hard UI choices.
- **Plan mode** (Shift+Tab) for M tickets. Start a new chat when switching tickets or when the agent repeats mistakes.
- **`scripts/agents/gate.sh` must pass before every push.** Open the PR with the template; never merge your own PR.
